    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d393">

                <pb facs="0462" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg402"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr.
                            Gresham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-26"><hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received March 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 268.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a copy and a translation
                    of the decree of February 24, forbidding the importation of American cattle into
                    France, the substance of which I telegraphed you on the 25th instant. It is
                    reported that the pretext under which this measure was taken was the prevalence
                    in the United States of Texas fever and pleuro-pneumonia. I inclose also a copy
                    of my telegram.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d393-a1.xml" xpointer="d393-a1"/>
            </div>
